{
  "_about": "Ask to be unmuted (12.1.17, D04.6). Byte-identical in web src/features/calls/unmuteask.vectors.json and desktop crates/app/src/testvectors/unmuteask.json. Wire: a LiveKit data packet, reliable, topic 'tinhat.unmute_ask', payload askPayload (exactly the bytes below), sent by a server-muted person to everyone in the call. The ASKER is the packet's SFU sender identity, never anything in the payload. Older clients (12.1.15 and before) have no branch for this topic and drop it. parse: a receiver decodes the packet bytes as UTF-8 (invalid sequences become U+FFFD) and drops ONE leading byte-order mark (U+FEFF); then true only for text of at most maxPayloadBytes bytes of UTF-8 that is a JSON object whose 'v' is a finite whole number >= 1 (other keys ignored, so later versions stay asks). cooldownLeft(lastAskMs|null, nowMs): ms until the asker's button works again (null or a clock that went backwards = 0). verdict: what a RECEIVER does with an ask, checked in this order: the asker is my own account -> ignore:self; I can't moderate calls here -> ignore:not-moderator; either rank unknown -> ignore:unknown-rank (fail closed); my rank is not above the asker's -> ignore:rank; the asker isn't server-muted -> ignore:not-muted; a toast for this asker less than toastGapMs ago (0 <= now-last) -> hand (refresh the hand, no toast); else toast (hand + toast). No verdict ever unmutes: Unmute is the moderator's own click, which goes through the server's moderation API (which checks rank again). handShown(askedAtMs, nowMs, stillMuted): stillMuted and now-askedAt < handMs. label(leftMs): the asker's button text. Wording: the same strings in both apps.",
  "topic": "tinhat.unmute_ask",
  "askPayload": "{\"v\":1}",
  "constants": {
    "askCooldownMs": 30000,
    "toastGapMs": 30000,
    "handMs": 60000,
    "undoMs": 5000,
    "maxPayloadBytes": 256,
    "askHoldMs": 10000
  },
