  "_aboutHold": "An ask that arrives before the receiver knows the asker is server-muted (the call server mutes them BEFORE the moderator's request returns and the moderator announces it) is HELD, not dropped: at most one per asker, only from someone in the call who isn't me, at most 64 held at once. When a mute record for that asker arrives (a mute packet, or my own mute of them), a held ask still live by heldAskLive(heldAtMs, nowMs) (0 <= now - heldAt < askHoldMs; a clock that went backwards drops it) is decided then, exactly like a fresh ask (the verdict above, the toast gap included). It's dropped when the asker leaves or the call ends. Holding never unmutes anyone and never shows anything by itself. heldScenarios run holdPut(held, id, nowMs, max) -> true = held (first drops every entry no longer live at nowMs; refuses a NEW asker when max are held; an asker already held gets the new time) and holdTake(held, id, nowMs) -> true = decide it now (the entry is removed either way) on one map, in order; the 4th element of each op is the expected result.",
