  "_aboutUndoOffered": "A moderator's mute request can finish late. undoOffered(prevRev|null, since): when my mute's answer comes back, for each identity it muted, prevRev = the revision of the record it replaces (null = none) and since = the highest revision handed out when my request went out (revisions only grow). The Undo is offered only when every identity gives prevRev == null or prevRev <= since; otherwise someone muted them after my request left (a newer mute my late answer would overwrite) and the toast shows its text without the Undo button. Read prevRev in the same step that records my mute.",
